{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"center","type":"text","text":"# The Kaufmann Paradox\n\n**Most cited. Most contradicted.**\n\nLoad-bearing hinges: #4, #6, #15, #18\n\nHis evidence is structural — the graph needs it.\nHis conclusions: 37+ contradiction edges, zero support.\n\nEither his evidence is stronger than acknowledged,\nor his interpretation is so flawed the evidence\nitself needs re-examination.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":-30,"y":-1040,"width":480,"height":400,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"rej-torah","type":"text","text":"## Torah Is Pre-Prophetic\n\n**Hinge #6 · 9 dependents**\n\nKaufmann: Pentateuch predates\nprophets. Prophets reform from\nan existing Mosaic law.\n\nContradicted by Documentary\nHypothesis, Josianic reform (622\nBCE), and Amos's silence on\nTorah legislation.\n\nConsensus: Torah reaches final\nform during/after exile.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]","x":2200,"y":-1360,"width":380,"height":440,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ev-prophets","type":"text","text":"## Prophetic Unanimity\n\nNot one prophet engages pagan\nmythology on its own terms.\n\nThey fight cultic practice, not\ntheology. Elijah at Carmel is a\npower contest, not a theological\ndebate. Isaiah 44 mocks idol\ncraftsmanship, not myth.\n\nGenuine textual feature.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]","x":-1640,"y":-1165,"width":380,"height":365,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"struct-consensus","type":"text","text":"## Kaufmann in the Consensus\n\nHis **observations** survive:\n- Bible uses fetishism polemic ✓\n- Bible lacks theogony ✓\n- Prophets don't engage pagan myth ✓\n\nHis **interpretation** doesn't:\n- That these prove non-mythological\n  origin is contradicted by 37+ edges.\n\nIndispensable and wrong.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]","x":-1640,"y":-2180,"width":400,"height":380,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ev-fetishism","type":"text","text":"## Fetishism Polemic\n\n**Hinge #4 · 10 direct / 30 cascade**\n\nBible characterizes paganism as\n\"wood and stone\" worship.\n\nProphets ridicule idols as manufactured\nobjects, not real deities.\n\nKaufmann's strongest empirical claim.\nEven critics accept the observation.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase1-hinge-inventory]]","x":-790,"y":-3240,"width":380,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ev-theogony","type":"text","text":"## Absence of Theogony\n\nBible lacks divine birth narratives,\nmetadivine realm, and mythology\nproper.\n\nNo Yahweh birth story.\nNo divine genealogy.\nNo theomachy.\n\nBut: Chaoskampf IS present (Ps 74,\nPs 89, Isa 51). Transformed, not absent.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]","x":1480,"y":-1930,"width":380,"height":370,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"rej-non-myth","type":"text","text":"## Israelite Religion\nNon-Mythological\n\n**Core thesis · contradicted by\nentire ANE evidence base**\n\nKaufmann defined \"mythology\" so\nnarrowly (theogony only) that he\nexcluded evidence by definition.\n\nChaoskampf, divine council, temple\nideology, covenant forms — all\nhave ANE parallels.\n\nCircular definition, not evidence.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]\n[[notes/theology/meta-analysis-scholars]]","x":2480,"y":290,"width":380,"height":470,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"struct-instability","type":"text","text":"## The Instability\n\n**Either:** Kaufmann is underrated —\nhis evidence is stronger than the\nfield acknowledges and the fetishism\npolemic hasn't been explained.\n\n**Or:** Kaufmann is fatally flawed — his\ninterpretive lens distorts everything,\nand 30+ claims built on his evidence\nare standing on sand.\n\nStructural integrity question of\nthe entire graph.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]","x":210,"y":-50,"width":400,"height":450,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"struct-schmid","type":"text","text":"## Schmid Resolution\n\nIf Schmid's late textual dating is\ncorrect, Kaufmann's evidence base\n**dissolves**:\n\n- Pentateuch post-exilic → \"original\n  monotheism\" is anachronistic\n- Prophetic corpus redacted late →\n  \"unanimity\" is editorial, not historical\n- Torah/prophet sequence reversed\n\n**Survival rate: 41%**\n\nParadox doesn't need solving —\nit needs dissolving.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":1270,"y":-90,"width":400,"height":530,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"rej-syncretism","type":"text","text":"## No Genuine Syncretism\n\n**4 contradiction edges**\n\nKaufmann: Israel never genuinely\nabsorbed foreign religion.\n\nContradicted by Kuntillet Ajrud\n(\"Yahweh and his Asherah\"),\nElephantine (Anat-Yahu), ~1000\nJudean Pillar Figurines, Psalm\n29 (Baal hymn reattributed).\n\nMaterial evidence is decisive.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase4-unknowns-and-convergence]]","x":-540,"y":100,"width":380,"height":460,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ev-no-foreign","type":"text","text":"## No Foreign God as\nActive Character\n\nOnly Yahweh acts in biblical\nnarrative. Foreign gods are\nnamed but never dramatized.\n\nContrast: Ugaritic, Mesopotamian,\nEgyptian texts all feature gods\nas active agents.\n\nSuppression, not ignorance.\nMonotheizing rhetoric at work.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/capstone-what-does-this-mean]]","x":-1300,"y":330,"width":380,"height":430,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"struct-cascade","type":"text","text":"## The Dependency Cascade\n\nFetishism (Hinge #4) feeds:\n\n```\n   Non-Mythological Thesis\n  /          |          \\\nNo Sync   Monotheism   Pre-Prop\n  \\          |          /\n   Fetishism Polemic (#4)\n         |\n   30 dependent claims\n```\n\nRemove the base, everything\nabove it falls. Kaufmann\ncannot be removed without\nstructural collapse.\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase2-cascade-trees]]","x":-790,"y":-2010,"width":380,"height":490,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"rej-monotheism","type":"text","text":"## Monotheism Was Original\n\n**5 contradiction edges**\n\nKaufmann: monotheism was Israel's\nfoundational breakthrough.\n\nContradicted by Exod 15:11, Deut\n32:8-9, Ps 82, and the full\narchaeological record.\n\nConsensus: monolatry → henotheism\n→ monotheism (Deutero-Isaiah, 6th c.)\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]","x":1400,"y":-3110,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"struct-isolated","type":"text","text":"## Kaufmann Isolated\n\n**37+ contradiction edges**\n**Zero support edges**\n\nEvery major conclusion contradicted\nby multiple scholars at HIGH\nconfidence: Smith, Romer, Day,\nDever, Cross — all reject him.\n\nStress test survival:\nHeiser 72% · Tigay 85%\n**Kaufmann: 41-58%**\n\n[[notes/synthesis/phase3-counter-position-stress-tests]]","x":520,"y":-2480,"width":400,"height":400,"color":"6"}
	],
